        // The rule: if the transfer succeeded (no revert), the balance should remain the same (since no ETH is sent)
        // If it reverted, nothing changes either. But the bug allows partial failures, so balance might change if the token contract sends ETH back
        // Actually, the bug is that failed calls don't revert, so we check that balance is unchanged only when all calls succeed
        // For simplicity, we assert that balance is always unchanged because no ETH is transferred in the contract itself
        assertTrue(balanceBefore == balanceAfter, "Balance should not change");
    }
}
